NetTime sets the clock from a network time server, and sets the Dreamcast's own
clock with it, so the time is right the next time it's switched on.

The Dreamcast keeps local time, and time servers give UTC, so fill in how many
hours you are from UTC: -8 for California, +1 for Paris, +5:30 for India. Tick
Summer time while the clocks are forward. Set clock asks the server and sets the
time. Save keeps the server and the offset on a VMU.

It needs the network up first, which a Broadband Adapter does by itself.
